# Build output
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe
*.so
*.dylib

# `go build ./tools/...` without -o drops a binary named after the package
# straight into the repo root. Name every tool explicitly so one of these
# never gets committed by accident.
/faultinjector
/corpusctl
/eval
/whymiss

# Test and coverage artifacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.*
/profile.cov

# Runtime state. whymiss owns a SQLite database with rolling retention (I-12);
# it is operator data, never repo content.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
/data/

# Local operator config. The committed defaults live in docs/configuration.md;
# a real deployment's config points at real endpoints and stays out of git.
/whymiss.yaml
/whymiss.local.yaml
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!**/.env.example
*.log

# Validator keys and secrets must never enter this repo (I-2). Mirrors the deny
# list in .claude/settings.json as defense in depth.
*keystore*
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/

# Agent tooling. The shared contracts (.claude/settings.json, .codex/config.toml)
# ARE committed — only per-developer overrides and logs are ignored.
.claude/settings.local.json
.codex-log/

# Editors and OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Nothing below internal/rca/testdata/ or test/corpus/ is ignored on purpose.
# Golden files and corpus scenarios are reviewed like production code
# (STRUCTURE.md: "test/corpus is not test scaffolding — it is an asset").
